  "Register values of an S3811 revision 1 (chip ID word 0x38110001) after a reset, read on a Comsat TE 1050 HD (dump.bin's board) through the v4 demo's 'md' after a watchdog restart into the original Opticum bootloader, before 'video init' (2026-11-12).  gen_video_init.py presets them in the emulator, whose device registers otherwise start at 0, so that the drivers' read-modify-write stores come out as on the chip.  Only the display engine (not the GMA layer, which the demo had set), the blocks at 0xB8007000, the TV encoder, VCAP, the HDMI transmitter (not its ID echoes, the interrupt source or the live hot-plug bits beyond what the recording forces anyway) and the clock words 0x60-0x6F / 0xA0-0xC3."
